<title>JAPAN: Yen weakness follows mark's fall - Japan govt.</title>
<headline>Yen weakness follows mark's fall - Japan govt.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-02-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>The recent weakness in the yen follows the mark's decline against the dollar because of the sluggish German economy, Japanese government spokesman Seiroku Kajiyama told a news conference on Thursday.  </p>
<p>&quot;The weakness of the yen is linked to the exchange rate between the U.S. dollar and the mark,&quot; Kajiyama said.</p>
<p>The dollar hit a 34-month high against the mark this week on worries about high unemployment rates in Germany and an increasingly tight fiscal policy there.</p>
</text>
